    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [x] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [x] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n- [x] I have updated 'mini.nvim' to latest version of the `main` branch\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.map\n\n### Neovim version\n\n0.10.x\n\n### Description\n\nWhen using the mini.map plugin, I noticed that the minimap window overlaps my winbar. Specifically, when the minimap window is open, part of the winbar content is obscured and cannot be fully displayed. \n\nI hope that the minimap window and winbar can coexist without interference. Ideally, the minimap window's display area should avoid overlapping the winbar, or a configuration option could be provided to allow users to customize the position and size of the minimap window, ensuring that the winbar content remains fully visible.\n\n### Reproduction\n\n1. Open Neovim and enable the mini.map plugin.\n2. Ensure that the winbar is enabled and its content extends to the position of the minimap.\n3. Open the minimap window and observe whether the winbar is being overlapped.",
